 parental consent\". That puts her on the parental-involvement side.\n- **Why no rung is seated:** the bill does not require schools to notify parents (rung 4). It does not require parental permission before staff use a different name or pronouns (rung 5). What it covers is the education record, and under H17 a rung's object is a clause. Its guarantee of record access only partly matches rung 3, and its consent clause goes beyond rung 3. So it separates the sides but not the rungs on that side.\n- **The vote:** House final passage was 59–6–10, so 6 of 75 members voted No. That is under 10%, so the vote is `near-unanimous` and can't carry a chair on its own.\n- **Time:** I coded all three records `in-term` under V5, because they come from her House service in the same legislature. Her current term dates are unknown, so code should confirm that.\n- **`needs_source`:** the House floor debate audio from 2/1/2023 (Day 16, SB100, Gricius). If she said anything there about notifying parents or about names and pronouns, those would be her own words and could seat a chair.\n\nThere are no candidate quotes, because none of the sources contain her own words.","ttft_ms":12565,"type":"result","duration_ms":30573,"uuid":"3f724b49-f413-4c79-b6c5-ff971a71b4b5","ttft_stream_ms":1294,"time_to_request_ms":73,"first_content_frame_ms":1294,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
